IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-definitions`

-- coa16-part20-minimum-capital.l4: the Companies Act 2006, Part 20 (Private and public companies), Chapter 2
-- (Minimum share capital requirement for public companies): ss 761 to 767 (lines 9885-9961 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".  Every `-- src:` line is generated by
-- srcrefs.py from that file (work/build.py), never retyped.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa16-part19-general.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING and their comments).
-- Imports coa-definitions (the keel's `s 4(2)` public company, called directly).
--
-- MONEY.  Pounds sterling unless the name says euros.  The sterling amount of the authorised minimum is the Act's
-- own figure (s 763(1)(a)); the prescribed euro equivalent and any amount substituted by an order under s 764 are
-- inputs, never guessed.  An order under s 764 would change the answers (s 763(6)).

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Part 20 -- Chapter 2: Minimum share capital requirement for public companies
-- =========================================================================================================

-- ---- s 761: Public company: requirement as to minimum share capital ---------------------------------------------

-- src:9886 | 761 Public company: requirement as to minimum share capital
-- src:9887 | (1) A company that is a public company (otherwise than by virtue of re-registration as a public company) must not do business or exercise any borrowing powers unless the registrar has issued it with a certificate under this section (a “trading certificate”).
-- src:9888 | (2) The registrar shall issue a trading certificate if, on an application made in accordance with section 762, he is satisfied that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum.
-- src:9889 | (3) For this purpose a share allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme shall not be taken into account unless paid up as to—
-- src:9890 | (a) at least one-quarter of the nominal value of the share, and
-- src:9891 | (b) the whole of any premium on the share.
-- src:9892 | (4) A trading certificate has effect from the date on which it is issued and is conclusive evidence that the company is entitled to do business and exercise any borrowing powers.
@ref s 761 Public company: requirement as to minimum share capital (src:9886-9892)
DECLARE `s 761 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 761 do business`
    `s 761 exercise a borrowing power`
    `s 761 issue the company with a trading certificate`

-- (1) "A company that is a public company (otherwise than by virtue of re-registration as a public company) must not do
-- business or exercise any borrowing powers unless the registrar has issued it with a certificate under this section
-- (a “trading certificate”)."  A bar that the registrar's certificate lifts ("unless"); a company outside the class
-- named in its own wording is not covered.
@ref s 761(1) Public company: the bar (src:9887)
GIVEN company IS A `Company profile`
      `the requirements as to registration or re-registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date (s 4(2)(b))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company by virtue of re-registration as a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar has issued the company with a trading certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 761(1) the company is barred from doing business or exercising any borrowing powers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(2) the company is a public company` company `the requirements as to registration or re-registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date (s 4(2)(b))`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the company is a public company by virtue of re-registration as a public company`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(otherwise than by virtue of re-registration as a public company)"
        ELSE IF `the registrar has issued the company with a trading certificate`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not do business or exercise any borrowing powers unless the registrar has issued it with a certificate under this section"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company that is a public company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): follows s 4

-- The bar as a regulative rule: a SHANT for each act, for a company the bar binds.
@ref s 761(1) Public company: the bar as a regulative rule (src:9887)
GIVEN `the company is barred (s 761(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 761 act`
`s 761(1) the company must not do business or exercise borrowing powers` MEANS
    IF (`the company is barred (s 761(1))`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN (PARTY Company
          SHANT `s 761 do business`
          HENCE FULFILLED
          LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 761(1): the company did business without a trading certificate")
         RAND
         (PARTY Company
          SHANT `s 761 exercise a borrowing power`
          HENCE FULFILLED
          LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 761(1): the company exercised a borrowing power without a trading certificate")
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (3) "For this purpose a share allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme shall not be taken into account
-- unless paid up as to (a) at least one-quarter of the nominal value of the share, and (b) the whole of any premium
-- on the share."  Whether a scheme is an employees' share scheme is the keel's s 1166: an input (BOOLEAN) here.
DECLARE `s 761(3) allotted share` HAS
    `s 761(3) the currency in which the share is denominated` IS A `s 765 currency`
    `s 761(3) the nominal value of the share` IS A NUMBER
    `s 761(3) the share was allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme (s 1166)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 761(3)(a) the amount paid up on the nominal value of the share` IS A NUMBER
    `s 761(3)(b) the premium on the share` IS A NUMBER
    `s 761(3)(b) the amount of the premium that has been paid` IS A NUMBER

@ref s 761(3) Public company: employees' share scheme shares (src:9889-9891)
GIVEN share IS A `s 761(3) allotted share`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 761(3) the scheme share is taken into account` MEANS
    IF share's `s 761(3) the share was allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme (s 1166)`
    THEN
        IF       share's `s 761(3)(a) the amount paid up on the nominal value of the share` AT LEAST ((share's `s 761(3) the nominal value of the share`) DIVIDED BY 4)
             AND share's `s 761(3)(b) the amount of the premium that has been paid` AT LEAST share's `s 761(3)(b) the premium on the share`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a share allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme shall not be taken into account unless paid up as to— (a) at least one-quarter of the nominal value of the share, and (b) the whole of any premium on the share"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a share allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme"

-- (2) A share counts towards "the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital" unless (3) leaves it out.
@ref s 761(2) Public company: which shares count (src:9888-9891)
GIVEN share IS A `s 761(3) allotted share`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 761(2) the share counts towards the nominal value of the allotted share capital` MEANS
    IF share's `s 761(3) the share was allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme (s 1166)`
    THEN `s 761(3) the scheme share is taken into account` share EQUALS JUST TRUE
    ELSE TRUE

-- (2)  of s 761: "The registrar shall issue a trading certificate if, on an application made in accordance with
-- section 762, he is satisfied that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the
-- authorised minimum."  Whether the requirement is in fact met is s 765(1); whether the registrar is satisfied is his.
@ref s 761(2) Public company: the requirement (src:9888)
GIVEN shares IS A LIST OF `s 761(3) allotted share`
      `the currency the company has elected` IS A `s 765 currency`
      `the sterling amount that an order under section 764 has substituted, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the prescribed euro equivalent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 761(2) the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum` MEANS
    `s 765(1) the initial requirement is met by reference to the currency` shares `the currency the company has elected` `the sterling amount that an order under section 764 has substituted, if there is one` `the prescribed euro equivalent`

@ref s 761(2) Public company: the registrar's duty (src:9888)
GIVEN `an application has been made in accordance with section 762` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar is satisfied that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 761(2) the registrar shall issue a trading certificate` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made in accordance with section 762` AND `the registrar is satisfied that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar shall issue a trading certificate if, on an application made in accordance with section 762, he is satisfied that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum"

@ref s 761(2) Public company: the registrar's duty as a regulative rule (src:9888)
GIVEN `the registrar shall issue a trading certificate (s 761(2))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 761 act`
`s 761(2) the registrar must issue the trading certificate` MEANS
    IF (`the registrar shall issue a trading certificate (s 761(2))`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN PARTY Registrar
         MUST `s 761 issue the company with a trading certificate`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (4) "A trading certificate has effect from the date on which it is issued and is conclusive evidence that the company
-- is entitled to do business and exercise any borrowing powers."
@ref s 761(4) Public company: the effect of the certificate (src:9892)
GIVEN `the date the trading certificate was issued, if one has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 761(4) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the company is entitled to do business and exercise any borrowing powers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the trading certificate was issued, if one has been`
    WHEN JUST issued THEN
        IF `the date on which the question is asked` AT LEAST issued
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trading certificate has effect from the date on which it is issued"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A trading certificate": no certificate has been issued

-- ---- s 762: Procedure for obtaining certificate -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9893 | 762 Procedure for obtaining certificate
-- src:9894 | (1) An application for a certificate under section 761 must—
-- src:9895 | (a) state that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum,
-- src:9896 | (b) specify the amount, or estimated amount, of the company's preliminary expenses,
-- src:9897 | (c) specify any amount or benefit paid or given, or intended to be paid or given, to any promoter of the company, and the consideration for the payment or benefit, ...
-- src:9898 | (d) be accompanied by a statement of compliance and
-- src:9899 | (e) be accompanied by a statement of the aggregate amount paid up on the shares of the company on account of their nominal value.
-- src:9900 | (2) The statement of compliance is a statement that the company meets the requirements for the issue of a certificate under section 761.
-- src:9901 | (3) The registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence of the matters stated in it.
@ref s 762 Procedure for obtaining certificate (src:9893-9901)
GIVEN `the application states that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application specifies the amount, or estimated amount, of the company's preliminary expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application specifies any amount or benefit paid or given, or intended to be paid or given, to any promoter of the company, and the consideration for the payment or benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by a statement of compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by a statement of the aggregate amount paid up on the shares of the company on account of their nominal value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 762(1) the application is made in accordance with section 762` MEANS
    IF       `the application states that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum`
         AND `the application specifies the amount, or estimated amount, of the company's preliminary expenses`
         AND `the application specifies any amount or benefit paid or given, or intended to be paid or given, to any promoter of the company, and the consideration for the payment or benefit`
         AND `the application is accompanied by a statement of compliance`
         AND `the application is accompanied by a statement of the aggregate amount paid up on the shares of the company on account of their nominal value`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application for a certificate under section 761 must— (a) state that the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is not less than the authorised minimum, (b) specify the amount, or estimated amount, of the company's preliminary expenses, (c) specify any amount or benefit paid or given, or intended to be paid or given, to any promoter of the company, and the consideration for the payment or benefit, (d) be accompanied by a statement of compliance and (e) be accompanied by a statement of the aggregate amount paid up on the shares of the company on account of their nominal value"

-- (2) "The statement of compliance is a statement that the company meets the requirements for the issue of a certificate
-- under section 761."  Read as a definition, closed (fork F18).
@ref s 762(2) Procedure for obtaining certificate: the statement of compliance (src:9900)
GIVEN `the statement says that the company meets the requirements for the issue of a certificate under section 761` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 762(2) the statement is the statement of compliance` MEANS
    IF `the statement says that the company meets the requirements for the issue of a certificate under section 761`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of compliance is a statement that the company meets the requirements for the issue of a certificate under section 761"

-- (3) "The registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence of the matters stated in it."
@ref s 762(3) Procedure for obtaining certificate: sufficient evidence (src:9901)
GIVEN `the statement is the statement of compliance (s 762(2))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 762(3) the registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence of the matters stated in it` MEANS
    IF (`the statement is the statement of compliance (s 762(2))`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar may accept the statement of compliance"

-- ---- s 763: The authorised minimum ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9902 | 763 The authorised minimum
-- src:9903 | (1) “The authorised minimum”, in relation to the nominal value of a public company's allotted share capital is—
-- src:9904 | (a) £50,000, or
-- src:9905 | (b) the prescribed euro equivalent.
-- src:9906 | (2) The Secretary of State may by order prescribe the amount in euros that is for the time being to be treated as equivalent to the sterling amount of the authorised minimum.
-- src:9907 | (3) This power may be exercised from time to time as appears to the Secretary of State to be appropriate.
-- src:9908 | (4) The amount prescribed shall be determined by applying an appropriate spot rate of exchange to the sterling amount and rounding to the nearest 100 euros.
-- src:9909 | (5) An order under this section is subject to negative resolution procedure.
-- src:9910 | (6) This section has effect subject to any exercise of the power conferred by section 764 (power to alter authorised minimum).
-- (1)(a) "£50,000".  The text's own figure; (6) makes it subject to any exercise of the power in s 764.
@ref s 763 The authorised minimum (src:9902-9910)
`s 763(1)(a) the sterling amount of the authorised minimum` MEANS 50_000

-- (6) "This section has effect subject to any exercise of the power conferred by section 764": a sterling amount that
-- an order under s 764 has substituted, if there is one, replaces the Act's figure.
@ref s 763(6) The authorised minimum: subject to section 764 (src:9910)
GIVEN `the sterling amount that an order under section 764 has substituted, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 763(6) the sterling amount of the authorised minimum, subject to any order under section 764` MEANS
    fromMaybe `s 763(1)(a) the sterling amount of the authorised minimum` `the sterling amount that an order under section 764 has substituted, if there is one`

-- (1) "“The authorised minimum”, in relation to the nominal value of a public company's allotted share capital is (a)
-- £50,000, or (b) the prescribed euro equivalent."  Which of the two is s 765(1): sterling share capital against
-- the sterling amount, euro share capital against the euro equivalent.
@ref s 763(1) The authorised minimum (src:9903-9905)
GIVEN currency IS A `s 765 currency`
      `the sterling amount that an order under section 764 has substituted, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the prescribed euro equivalent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 763(1) the authorised minimum in the currency` MEANS
    CONSIDER currency
    WHEN `s 765 sterling` THEN JUST (`s 763(6) the sterling amount of the authorised minimum, subject to any order under section 764` `the sterling amount that an order under section 764 has substituted, if there is one`)
    WHEN `s 765 euros` THEN JUST `the prescribed euro equivalent`
    WHEN `s 765 another currency` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text fixes the authorised minimum in sterling and in euros only

-- (4) "The amount prescribed shall be determined by applying an appropriate spot rate of exchange to the sterling
-- amount and rounding to the nearest 100 euros."  The text does not say how a tie is rounded; half rounds up here (fork F19).
-- (The power to prescribe by order, (2), (3) and (5), is machinery: inert, reason 2.)
@ref s 763(4) The authorised minimum: how the euro amount is determined (src:9908)
GIVEN `the sterling amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the spot rate of exchange, in euros to the pound` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 763(4) the euro amount prescribed for a spot rate` MEANS
    (FLOOR ((((`the sterling amount` TIMES `the spot rate of exchange, in euros to the pound`) DIVIDED BY 100) PLUS 0.5))) TIMES 100

-- ---- s 764: Power to alter authorised minimum --------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9911 | 764 Power to alter authorised minimum
-- src:9912 | (1) The Secretary of State may by order—
-- src:9913 | (a) alter the sterling amount of the authorised minimum, and
-- src:9914 | (b) make a corresponding alteration of the prescribed euro equivalent.
-- src:9915 | (2) The amount of the prescribed euro equivalent shall be determined by applying an appropriate spot rate of exchange to the sterling amount and rounding to the nearest 100 euros.
-- src:9916 | (3) An order under this section that increases the authorised minimum may—
-- src:9917 | (a) require a public company having an allotted share capital of which the nominal value is less than the amount specified in the order to—
-- src:9918 | (i) increase that value to not less than that amount, or
-- src:9919 | (ii) re-register as a private company;
-- src:9920 | (b) make provision in connection with any such requirement for any of the matters for which provision is made by this Act relating to—
-- src:9921 | (i) a company's registration, re-registration or change of name,
-- src:9922 | (ii) payment for shares comprised in a company's share capital, and
-- src:9923 | (iii) offers to the public of shares in or debentures of a company,
-- src:9924 | including provision as to the consequences (in criminal law or otherwise) of a failure to comply with any requirement of the order;
-- src:9925 | (c) provide for any provision of the order to come into force on different days for different purposes.
-- src:9926 | (4) An order under this section is subject to affirmative resolution procedure.
@ref s 764 Power to alter authorised minimum (src:9911-9926)
GIVEN `the sterling amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the spot rate of exchange, in euros to the pound` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 764(2) the euro amount prescribed for a spot rate` MEANS
    (FLOOR ((((`the sterling amount` TIMES `the spot rate of exchange, in euros to the pound`) DIVIDED BY 100) PLUS 0.5))) TIMES 100

-- (3)(a) "An order under this section that increases the authorised minimum may (a) require a public company having an
-- allotted share capital of which the nominal value is less than the amount specified in the order to (i) increase
-- that value to not less than that amount, or (ii) re-register as a private company".  What an order may do to a
-- company is a liability of the company; the power to make the order is machinery (inert, reason 2).
@ref s 764(3) Power to alter authorised minimum: an order that increases the minimum (src:9916-9919)
GIVEN `the order increases the authorised minimum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is less than the amount specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 764(3)(a) the order may require the company to increase its capital or re-register as a private company` MEANS
    IF `the order increases the authorised minimum` AND `the company is a public company` AND `the nominal value of the company's allotted share capital is less than the amount specified in the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order under this section that increases the authorised minimum may (a) require a public company having an allotted share capital of which the nominal value is less than the amount specified in the order"

-- ---- s 765: Authorised minimum: application of initial requirement ---------------------------------------------------

-- src:9927 | 765 Authorised minimum: application of initial requirement
-- src:9928 | (1) The initial requirement for a public company to have allotted share capital of a nominal value not less than the authorised minimum, that is—
-- src:9929 | (a) the requirement in section 761(2) for the issue of a trading certificate, or
-- src:9930 | (b) the requirement in section 91(1)(a) for re-registration as a public company,
-- src:9931 | must be met either by reference to allotted share capital denominated in sterling or by reference to allotted share capital denominated in euros (but not partly in one and partly in the other).
-- src:9932 | (2) Whether the requirement is met is determined in the first case by reference to the sterling amount and in the second case by reference to the prescribed euro equivalent.
-- src:9933 | (3) No account is to be taken of any allotted share capital of the company denominated in a currency other than sterling or, as the case may be, euros.
-- src:9934 | (4) If the company could meet the requirement either by reference to share capital denominated in sterling or by reference to share capital denominated in euros, it must elect in its application for a trading certificate or, as the case may be, for re-registration as a public company which is to be the currency by reference to which the matter is determined.
@ref s 765 Authorised minimum: application of initial requirement (src:9927-9934)
DECLARE `s 765 currency` IS ONE OF
    `s 765 sterling`
    `s 765 euros`
    `s 765 another currency`

-- s 765(3): "No account is to be taken of any allotted share capital of the company denominated in a currency other
-- than sterling or, as the case may be, euros", and s 765(1): not partly in one and partly in the other.
@ref s 765(3) Authorised minimum: application of initial requirement: other currencies (src:9933)
GIVEN shares IS A LIST OF `s 761(3) allotted share`
      currency IS A `s 765 currency`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 765(3) the nominal value of the allotted share capital that counts in the currency` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN share YIELD share's `s 761(3) the nominal value of the share`)
             (filter (GIVEN share YIELD (share's `s 761(3) the currency in which the share is denominated`) EQUALS currency AND `s 761(2) the share counts towards the nominal value of the allotted share capital` share) shares))

@ref s 765(1) Authorised minimum: application of initial requirement (src:9928-9932)
GIVEN shares IS A LIST OF `s 761(3) allotted share`
      currency IS A `s 765 currency`
      `the sterling amount that an order under section 764 has substituted, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the prescribed euro equivalent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 765(1) the initial requirement is met by reference to the currency` MEANS
    CONSIDER currency
    WHEN `s 765 sterling` THEN
        IF `s 765(3) the nominal value of the allotted share capital that counts in the currency` shares `s 765 sterling` AT LEAST `s 763(6) the sterling amount of the authorised minimum, subject to any order under section 764` `the sterling amount that an order under section 764 has substituted, if there is one`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be met either by reference to allotted share capital denominated in sterling or by reference to allotted share capital denominated in euros (but not partly in one and partly in the other)" (the sterling share capital is below the sterling amount, s 765(2))
    WHEN `s 765 euros` THEN
        IF `s 765(3) the nominal value of the allotted share capital that counts in the currency` shares `s 765 euros` AT LEAST `the prescribed euro equivalent`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be met either by reference to allotted share capital denominated in sterling or by reference to allotted share capital denominated in euros (but not partly in one and partly in the other)" (the euro share capital is below the prescribed euro equivalent, s 765(2))
    WHEN `s 765 another currency` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be met either by reference to allotted share capital denominated in sterling or by reference to allotted share capital denominated in euros"

-- (4) "If the company could meet the requirement either by reference to share capital denominated in sterling or by
-- reference to share capital denominated in euros, it must elect in its application for a trading certificate or, as
-- the case may be, for re-registration as a public company which is to be the currency by reference to which the
-- matter is determined."  A duty whose "if" is unmet does not arise: not covered (fork F8).
@ref s 765(4) Authorised minimum: application of initial requirement: the election (src:9934)
GIVEN shares IS A LIST OF `s 761(3) allotted share`
      `the sterling amount that an order under section 764 has substituted, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the prescribed euro equivalent` IS A NUMBER
      `the company has elected, in its application, which currency is to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 765(4) the company has made the election the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       ((`s 765(1) the initial requirement is met by reference to the currency` shares `s 765 sterling` `the sterling amount that an order under section 764 has substituted, if there is one` `the prescribed euro equivalent`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
         AND ((`s 765(1) the initial requirement is met by reference to the currency` shares `s 765 euros` `the sterling amount that an order under section 764 has substituted, if there is one` `the prescribed euro equivalent`) EQUALS (JUST TRUE))
    THEN
        IF `the company has elected, in its application, which currency is to be used`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must elect in its application for a trading certificate or, as the case may be, for re-registration as a public company which is to be the currency by reference to which the matter is determined"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the company could meet the requirement either by reference to share capital denominated in sterling or by reference to share capital denominated in euros"

-- ---- s 767: Consequences of doing business etc without a trading certificate ---------------------------------------------------

-- src:9950 | 767 Consequences of doing business etc without a trading certificate
-- src:9951 | (1) If a company does business or exercises any borrowing powers in contravention of section 761, an offence is committed by—
-- src:9952 | (a) the company, and
-- src:9953 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:9954 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (1) is liable—
-- src:9955 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:9956 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
-- src:9957 | (3) A contravention of section 761 does not affect the validity of a transaction entered into by the company, but if a company—
-- src:9958 | (a) enters into a transaction in contravention of that section, and
-- src:9959 | (b) fails to comply with its obligations in connection with the transaction within 21 days from being called on to do so,
-- src:9960 | the directors of the company are jointly and severally liable to indemnify any other party to the transaction in respect of any loss or damage suffered by him by reason of the company's failure to comply with its obligations.
-- src:9961 | (4) The directors who are so liable are those who were directors at the time the company entered into the transaction.
@ref s 767 Consequences of doing business etc without a trading certificate (src:9950-9961)
DECLARE `s 767(1) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 767(1) the company`
    `s 767(1) an officer of the company` HAS `s 767(1) the officer is in default (s 1121)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 767(1) another person`

-- (1) "If a company does business or exercises any borrowing powers in contravention of section 761, an offence is
-- committed by (a) the company, and (b) every officer of the company who is in default."
@ref s 767(1) Doing business without a trading certificate: the offence (src:9951-9953)
GIVEN company IS A `Company profile`
      `the requirements as to registration or re-registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date (s 4(2)(b))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company by virtue of re-registration as a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar has issued the company with a trading certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company does business or exercises borrowing powers` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 767(1) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 767(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 761(1) the company is barred from doing business or exercising any borrowing powers` company `the requirements as to registration or re-registration as a public company have been complied with on or after the relevant date (s 4(2)(b))` `the company is a public company by virtue of re-registration as a public company` `the registrar has issued the company with a trading certificate`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company does business or exercises any borrowing powers in contravention of section 761, an offence is committed by": a trading certificate has been issued
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 761(1) does not govern the company
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT (`the company does business or exercises borrowing powers`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company does business or exercises any borrowing powers in contravention of section 761, an offence is committed by"
        ELSE
            CONSIDER person
            WHEN `s 767(1) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `s 767(1) an officer of the company` inDefault THEN
                CONSIDER inDefault
                WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121
            WHEN `s 767(1) another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and its officers in default

-- (2) "A person guilty of an offence under subsection (1) is liable (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine; (b) on
-- summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum."  A summary conviction in any of the three
-- places is a summary conviction.
@ref s 767(2) Doing business without a trading certificate: the penalty (src:9954-9956)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 767(2) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
    OTHERWISE Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `how the person is convicted`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- (3) "A contravention of section 761 does not affect the validity of a transaction entered into by the company".
@ref s 767(3) Doing business without a trading certificate: validity (src:9957)
GIVEN `the company entered into the transaction in contravention of section 761` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 767(3) the contravention of section 761 affects the validity of the transaction` MEANS
    IF `the company entered into the transaction in contravention of section 761`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A contravention of section 761 does not affect the validity of a transaction entered into by the company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a transaction entered into by the company" in contravention of section 761

-- (3) "... but if a company (a) enters into a transaction in contravention of that section, and (b) fails to comply with
-- its obligations in connection with the transaction within 21 days from being called on to do so, the directors of
-- the company are jointly and severally liable to indemnify any other party to the transaction in respect of any loss
-- or damage suffered by him by reason of the company's failure to comply with its obligations."  The days are whole
-- days from the day the company is called on; the twenty-first day is within the period.  A company that has not yet
-- complied while the 21 days are not up has not yet failed.
@ref s 767(3) Doing business without a trading certificate: the directors' liability (src:9957-9960)
GIVEN `the company entered into a transaction in contravention of section 761` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has complied with its obligations in connection with the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days from the company being called on to comply to the day it complied, or to now if it has not complied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 767(3) the directors are jointly and severally liable to indemnify the other party to the transaction` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company entered into a transaction in contravention of section 761`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but if a company (a) enters into a transaction in contravention of that section"
    ELSE IF `the days from the company being called on to comply to the day it complied, or to now if it has not complied` GREATER THAN 21
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the company has complied with its obligations in connection with the transaction`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) fails to comply with its obligations in connection with the transaction within 21 days from being called on to do so"
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 21 days have not run out and the company has not yet complied, so there is no answer yet

DECLARE `s 767 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 767 comply with the obligations in connection with the transaction`
    `s 767 indemnify the other party to the transaction`

-- The same as a regulative rule: the company must comply within 21 days (day 0 = being called on); if it does not, the
-- directors must indemnify the other party (no time is stated for that).
@ref s 767(3) Doing business without a trading certificate: the directors' liability as a regulative rule (src:9957-9960)
GIVEN `the company entered into a transaction in contravention of section 761` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 767 act`
`s 767(3) the company must comply with its obligations, failing which the directors must indemnify` MEANS
    IF `the company entered into a transaction in contravention of section 761`
    THEN PARTY Company
         MUST `s 767 comply with the obligations in connection with the transaction`
         WITHIN 21
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST (PARTY Director
               MUST `s 767 indemnify the other party to the transaction`
               HENCE FULFILLED
               LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "s 767(3): the directors did not indemnify the other party to the transaction")
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (4) "The directors who are so liable are those who were directors at the time the company entered into the
-- transaction."  Whether a person is a director is s 250 (coa5), an input.  "are those" closes the class (fork F13).
@ref s 767(4) Doing business without a trading certificate: which directors (src:9961)
GIVEN `the person occupied the position of director at the time the company entered into the transaction (s 250)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 767(4) the person is one of the directors who are liable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person occupied the position of director at the time the company entered into the transaction (s 250)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors who are so liable are those who were directors at the time the company entered into the transaction"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person was a director is s 250

-- (3) and (4) together: the directors "so liable" are those who were directors when the company entered into the
-- transaction.  A person who was not a director then is outside the class whatever the company did; a person who was
-- is liable when subsection (3) says the directors are.
@ref s 767(4) Doing business without a trading certificate: a director's liability (src:9957-9961)
GIVEN `the company entered into a transaction in contravention of section 761` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has complied with its obligations in connection with the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days from the company being called on to comply to the day it complied, or to now if it has not complied` IS A NUMBER
      `the person occupied the position of director at the time the company entered into the transaction (s 250)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 767(4) the director is liable to indemnify the other party to the transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 767(4) the person is one of the directors who are liable` `the person occupied the position of director at the time the company entered into the transaction (s 250)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors who are so liable are those who were directors at the time the company entered into the transaction"
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 767(3) the directors are jointly and severally liable to indemnify the other party to the transaction` `the company entered into a transaction in contravention of section 761` `the company has complied with its obligations in connection with the transaction` `the days from the company being called on to comply to the day it complied, or to now if it has not complied`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `s 767(3) the directors are jointly and severally liable to indemnify the other party to the transaction` `the company entered into a transaction in contravention of section 761` `the company has complied with its obligations in connection with the transaction` `the days from the company being called on to comply to the day it complied, or to now if it has not complied`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but if a company (a) enters into a transaction in contravention of that section, and (b) fails to comply with its obligations in connection with the transaction within 21 days from being called on to do so, the directors of the company are jointly and severally liable" (not met, whoever the person is)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person was a director at the time is s 250
